                "firstName": "J.",
                "lastName": "Hers"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "This paper discusses the need for accurate measurement of Broadcast Transmitter frequencies. This accuracy can be obtained only by a combination of many different methods, of which the most important are briefly described. Direct counting gives an absolute measurement and is used for checking standard frequency sources. Direct reading instruments can be checked against these. For higher accuracy harmonics of a standard frequency are generated, and an unknown frequency is measured by comparing it to one of these. The paper discusses various kinds of frequency standards, the generation of standard harmonic series, and their use in measurement. Various kinds of measuring equipment are described, with particular reference to the equipment built by the S.A.B.C.",
